{#
	About page (GLOSSARY: the collective's identity page), one page per language
	version (ADR-0002). `src/acerca-de.md` paginates over the site's languages,
	so this layout renders once per language and draws that version's own
	biography and team list. `lang` is the pagination alias; the language
	version is the content object under its code.

	The English object is optional at every level, and the CMS deletes a field
	an editor clears, so each field is read through the `localizedText` filter:
	the page's own value when it is written, otherwise the Spanish one,
	silently (GLOSSARY: Untranslated field). A cleared English About page is
	therefore complete and Spanish, never empty and never a broken build.

	Each team list stays one rich-text field so editors keep free-form control
	over names, roles and the former-collaborators heading, in that language
	only. The heading is hidden, the way the homepage and the archive name their
	page, since the About design has no visible title.
#}
{%- set versions = { es: es, en: en } -%}
<article class="about">
	<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ versions | localizedText(lang.code, "title") }}</h1>
	<div class="about-main">
		<div class="about-bio">{{ versions | localizedText(lang.code, "bio") | md | safe }}</div>
		<div class="about-team">{{ versions | localizedText(lang.code, "team") | md | safe }}</div>
	</div>
</article>
